      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-03T09:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not pushing back on the patch series, or anything,\nit just looks to me that using the same request pool and batch-size knob approach for async read makes sense. So that we can control IO pressure of async read and write in the same way. Just a symmetrical approach.",
      "parentUuid": "d24978d1_461f003f",
