      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T11:06:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think we need to improve our patch review process then.\n\nWell, at least for major features.\n\nLet me expand on this:\n\n\u003e However, my concern is our tendency to make things more\n\u003e complicated than necessary from the outset.\n\nWhile I agree that I have a tendency to complicate things for no apparent reason (no sarcasm), I can assure you the writeback in-flight knob was not such a thing. I simply was not aware of submit_bio() throttling back then. I found out about it only recently (clearly, I started this whole thread because I still didn\u0027t know about it at that point). So when I added that knob I believed that it was solving a real problem, not a \"what if\" one.\n\nNow, in my defense. That knob existed for a while in private patches, it also existed from day 1 in upstream submissions. We even had an upstream discussion on what would be the best default value - 32. Which re-assured me that we were addressing real problems, once again.\n\nI still like that knob. I look at it as a \"soft limit\", while HW queue depth is a \"hard limit\", so to speak.",
      "parentUuid": "eb410b63_3f3e6850",
